From e6e04f3309ee7b2059d71909019a3adae6e2528c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dongrez1990-cloud <dongrez1990-cloud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:12:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] UEFI (WinX): Erista Wi-Fi/BT bring-up, power, SD and boot
 handoff

Work that was sitting uncommitted in this tree:

- Drivers/WifiBtApp: Wi-Fi+BT bring-up for the original Switch (Erista). New
  t210/ stage headers, WifiLog.h, rebuilt PCIe/PHY stage tables (WifiPexStages.h,
  WifiPcie.h), WifiPrepare.h/.inf hookups.
- Library/PlatformBootManagerLib: new WifiHandoff.c so the UEFI stage hands the
  firmware RSS/CLM state to the Windows driver instead of leaving the station
  half-open; PlatformBm.c/.h/.inf wiring and LiteHomeBoot.c cleanup.
- Drivers/SdMmcDxe/SdMmc.c: SD path changes.
- AcpiTables/Dsdt/Dsdt.asl + WifiBtApp/t214/power.h: ACPI/power table updates.
- NintendoSwitch.dsc: platform description now builds the above.

Verified on hardware: Windows on Switch (Erista) reaches the desktop and the
Wi-Fi station connects; driver-side detail is in the Windows-for-Switch-Drivers
branch erista-0.7.x.
